CDNCA proxy_download_rate_shared.  Original CDNCA change, not upstream.
proxy_download_rate limits each session on its own, evaluated once when
the upstream connects; a market subscription's bandwidth (ADR 0012 ML-07)
is one budget for all of its sessions on the node, so a per-session share
fixed at entry let two sessions take 1.5 times the budget (L4F-E02).
proxy_download_rate_shared zone=name:size key: sessions with the same
non-empty key draw upstream bytes from one token bucket in shared memory,
refilled at proxy_download_rate bytes per second, at most one second's
worth stored (the burst); a reader waits on the event timer until a tenth
of a second's worth is available.  Without the directive, with an empty
key or no memory for the key, proxy_download_rate keeps its stock
per-session semantics.

